From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:20:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Start the Glymur USB4 PHY only once it
 is programmed

The Glymur USB4 and TBT3 sequences are written in the order of the
platform firmware's tables. A third of the way through, those take the
USB4 PCS out of software reset and set SERDES_START and PCS_START; the
PCS registers, both lanes and the board's RX equalisation follow. The PHY
therefore starts up while the rest of its configuration is still being
written.

That goes unnoticed as long as the writes are quick. When the thread is
held up for about a millisecond among the lane registers at boot, the PCS
never reports ready: PCS_STATUS reads 0x41 and stays there for at least
another 100 ms, phy_init() fails with -ETIMEDOUT and the host router is
not started until the partner is plugged in again. One reset pulse of the
PCS after the sequence makes it ready.

Seen on a Surface Laptop 8 at boot with the debug messages for the
register writes enabled, which stretch the sequence to about 1 ms: all
four failed router starts recorded have a gap of 1.0 to 1.4 ms among the
lane registers, and seven of the eight good ones have none. A sleep of
1 ms put after one lane register on purpose makes both routers fail at
boot in the old order, and neither with this change. The same sleep when
a partner is plugged in later does no harm in either order.

Keep the USB4 PCS in reset while the sequence is written, drop the reset
release and the start from the two tables, and leave both to the code
after the sequence, which did them a second time already. That is the
order in which the other QMP PHYs are brought up.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c              | 8 ++++++++
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-glymur-usb4-tables.h | 7 +++----
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index ba05d9680..9eca19f57 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4685,6 +4685,14 @@ static int qmp_v8_configure_usb4_phy(struct qmp_combo *qmp)
 	writel(SW_RESET, qmp->com + QPHY_V3_DP_COM_SW_RESET);
 	writel(SW_RESET, qmp->pcs + qmp->cfg->regs[QPHY_SW_RESET]);
 
+	/*
+	 * Hold the USB4 PCS in reset until the whole sequence is written. Let
+	 * go and started part of the way through, it comes up while the rest
+	 * is still being written, and when those writes are held up for about
+	 * a millisecond it never reports ready.
+	 */
+	writel(SW_RESET, qmp->usb4_pcs + qmp->cfg->regs[QPHY_SW_RESET]);
+
 	/* First record preserves the DP tunnel clock bit; retain all other order. */
 	writel(table[0].val | tunnel_clock, qmp->com + table[0].offset);
 	qmp_configure(qmp->dev, qmp->com, table + 1, count - 1);
diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-glymur-usb4-tables.h b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-glymur-usb4-tables.h
index 86ea849b6..fcca768c8 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-glymur-usb4-tables.h
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-glymur-usb4-tables.h
@@ -3,6 +3,9 @@
  * Glymur USB4 and TBT3 PHY programming sequences, in write order.
  * Offsets are relative to the start of the QMP combo PHY register space,
  * not to its sub-blocks.
+ *
+ * The sequences do not take the USB4 PCS out of software reset or start it:
+ * qmp_v8_configure_usb4_phy() does that once everything is written.
  */
 
 static const struct qmp_phy_init_tbl glymur_usb4_init_tbl[] = {
@@ -79,9 +82,7 @@ static const struct qmp_phy_init_tbl glymur_usb4_init_tbl[] = {
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x32f0, 0x25),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x32f4, 0x33),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x32fc, 0xaf),
-	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x3800, 0x00),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x3840, 0x01),
-	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x3844, 0x03),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x38ac, 0xcf),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x38b0, 0x0f),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x38e4, 0x03),
@@ -328,9 +329,7 @@ static const struct qmp_phy_init_tbl glymur_tbt3_init_tbl[] = {
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x32f0, 0x25),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x32f4, 0x33),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x32fc, 0xaf),
-	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x3800, 0x00),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x3840, 0x01),
-	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x3844, 0x03),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x38ac, 0xcf),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x38b0, 0x1f),
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(0x38e4, 0x03),
